Alembic migration directory for BK ClinicQ.

Database: PostgreSQL with PostGIS (required for geo features). Migrations assume
PostgreSQL; DATABASE_URL must be a PostgreSQL connection.

Schema
------
The platform host runs several products against one PostgreSQL database, so this
project keeps everything in a schema of its own — named by ``DB_SCHEMA``
(``src.commons.enums.DbSchema``, ``properties``) — and leaves ``public`` to PostGIS.
That covers the application tables *and* Alembic's own ``alembic_version``, which
``env.py`` places there via ``version_table_schema``.

Autogenerate reflects only that schema (``include_schemas`` plus the ``include_name``
filter in ``env.py``), so a diff can never propose dropping another product's tables.

Layout
------
- env.py           -> Alembic environment (uses src.core.config, src.database.models)
- script.py.mako   -> Template for new revisions; pre-wires the SCHEMA constant
- versions/        -> Migrations
                      0001 create the application schema
                      0002 baseline tables (user, rbac_role, role_permission,
                           refresh_token)

Note: versions/ is deliberately not a Python package. An ``__init__.py`` here would
make this directory importable as ``alembic`` and shadow the installed library
whenever the project root is on PYTHONPATH — which is exactly what the scripts below
do.

Running
-------
Migrations use DATABASE_URL from .env. Run from the project root:
  ./scripts/db/alembic-upgrade.sh              # upgrade to head
  ./scripts/db/alembic-revision.sh "message"   # new (empty) revision
  ./scripts/db/alembic-downgrade.sh -1         # roll back one step

Downgrading to base drops the tables but leaves the schema itself in place; see the
note in versions/0001_create_app_schema.py.
